# Regenerated staging trees produced by the stage chain (tools/stages/run_stages.py).
# The corrected corpus is promoted into data/media by `make promote`; the staging
# trees themselves are build output and are never committed.
data/_rebuild/

# Local source cache re-acquired by tools/fetch_sources.py. The payloads are large
# and licence-encumbered; data/_sources/MANIFEST.json (the provenance ledger) IS
# committed, the payloads are not.
data/_sources/**
!data/_sources/README.md
!data/_sources/MANIFEST.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# pytest
.pytest_cache/

# The bulk streaming exports. GitHub Pages publishes this repository's ROOT and
# refuses a published site over 1 GiB. media.sqlite.gz and the media.jsonl shards
# are a second and third encoding of data/media — which is itself published, and
# must stay published, because assets/media.js fetches data/media/<id>.json at
# runtime — and they measured 24.1 + 83.9 + 64.8 = 172.8 MiB, a sixth of the whole
# budget spent on redundancy. `make release-assets` now builds them into dist/ and
# they are distributed as assets on the `data-v1` release.
#
# Nothing became unreachable. data/api/manifest.json -> bulk_download names the
# release, the URL and the one command that fetches it; the parquet pair stays in
# the repository and DuckDB queries it over HTTP; every full record stays fetchable
# at data/media/<id>.json; and pymediadb.iter_full_records() streams the release
# and falls back to the per-medium endpoint when it is unreachable.
data/api/media.jsonl.gz
data/api/media.jsonl.part*.gz
data/api/media.sqlite.gz
dist/

# Local scratch: the legacy --report-only output of tools/stages/remap_components.py
# and the working backups taken before destructive steps.
build/
_backups/
_backup_naming_20260906/
